/* ---------- 城市总结段(v194,Ray 提议) ----------
   键 = GEO_CITY 的中文城市名,值 = [中文, English]。一座城一段,渲染在城市名下方、
   文明列表上方——与文明卡的总结段(CIVS.d)同一个位置、同一个作用。

   ⚠ 这一层要回答的**不是**「这里先后有过哪些朝代」——那是下面的文明列表和
   PLACE_LORE(键为「城市|文明」)已经在做的事,重复写等于把同一件事说三遍。
   这一段要回答的是:**这座城为什么在这里、它在历史上反复扮演什么角色、留下了什么**。
   写法:两三句,地理先行(为什么是这儿而不是隔壁)、角色其次、遗产收尾;
   只写查证过的硬事实,年代拿不准就 hedge;不写「自古以来」这类空话。

   表可以不全——没条目的城市什么都不渲染(audit 规则 58 拦孤儿键与非双语)。 */
const CITY_LORE = {
/* 中国 */
'西安': ['关中被山河围成一个天然的盒子,进可攻、退可守——周、秦、汉、唐都选在这里开国,做首都的年头在中国城市里最长。丝绸之路从这里出发;唐长安的棋盘格规划,日本照着修了平城京和平安京。',
 'The Guanzhong basin is a natural box walled in by mountains and rivers, easy to hold and easy to march out from — the Zhou, Qin, Han and Tang all founded their states here, and no Chinese city has served as capital for longer. The Silk Road set out from here, and Japan copied the grid plan of Tang Chang\'an at Nara and Kyoto.'],
'洛阳': ['「天下之中」:四方来朝的路程都差不多,东周到北宋十三个王朝在这里建都。它比西安更好养活,也更难守——无险可依,一旦中原失序，它总是最先被打烂的那座城。白马寺是佛教进中原的第一站,龙门石窟就凿在城南的崖壁上。',
 'The middle of everywhere: journeys from all quarters took about the same time, and thirteen dynasties from the Eastern Zhou to the Northern Song made it their capital. It was easier to feed than Xi\'an and harder to defend — with no natural barrier, it was always the first city wrecked when the central plain lost order. The White Horse Temple is where Buddhism entered China, and the Longmen grottoes are cut into the cliffs just south of town.'],
'北京': ['背靠燕山、面朝华北平原,是农耕世界与草原世界之间的门轴——辽、金、元、明、清都看中这一点,把一座边镇变成了首都。八百年里它反复被同一件事定义:谁掌握这里,谁就同时管着长城两边。',
 'Backed by the Yan mountains and facing the north China plain, it is the hinge between the farming world and the steppe — the Liao, Jin, Yuan, Ming and Qing all saw it and turned a frontier town into a capital. For eight centuries one fact has defined it: whoever holds this place governs both sides of the Great Wall at once.'],
'南京': ['长江在这里拐弯,山环水抱,北方一败就往这里退——东吴、东晋、南朝、南唐、明初、民国都在此落脚。它是中国最典型的「偏安之都」,也因此几度被屠城。',
 'The Yangtze bends here among hills and water, and when the north collapsed people fell back to it — the Wu, Eastern Jin, Southern Dynasties, Southern Tang, early Ming and the Republic all set up here. It is the classic Chinese capital of retreat, and it has been sacked for that more than once.'],
'杭州': ['钱塘江与大运河在这里交汇,一个西湖把城养成了园林——南宋定都之后,它是当时世界上最大最富的城市之一。丝绸、茶、印刷与文人趣味在这里合成一种生活方式,至今没散。',
 'The Qiantang river meets the Grand Canal here, and a single lake turned the city into a garden — after the Southern Song made it their capital it was among the largest and richest cities on earth. Silk, tea, printing and literati taste fused here into a way of living that has not dispersed since.'],
'开封': ['黄河边的平原,一道天险也没有,却因为运河成了北宋的首都——那是当时世界最大的城市,《清明上河图》画的就是它。无险可守,金兵一到就完;后来黄河改道,把整座旧城埋在地下六米。',
 'A plain by the Yellow River with not one natural defence, yet the canal made it the Northern Song capital — then the largest city in the world, and the one painted in Along the River During Qingming. With nothing to defend it, the Jin armies ended it; later the river changed course and buried the old city six metres down.'],
'成都': ['四面是山,中间一片被都江堰驯服的平原——两千三百年不改的水利,养出「天府之国」。离中原够远,所以乱世是退路(蜀汉、前后蜀、抗战陪都),太平时是最会过日子的地方。',
 'Ringed by mountains around a plain tamed by the Dujiangyan works — irrigation unchanged for 2,300 years made this the land of abundance. Far enough from the central plain to be a refuge in troubled times (Shu Han, the two Shu kingdoms, the wartime capital), and in quiet times the place that lives best.'],
'广州': ['珠江口的第一个大港,两千年没断过对外贸易——从南越国、唐代的蕃坊,到清代唯一开放的十三行。中国最早的清真寺、最早的洋行、最早成批出洋的人,多半从这里起步。',
 'The first great port at the mouth of the Pearl River, trading abroad without a break for two thousand years — from the kingdom of Nanyue to the Tang foreign quarter to the Thirteen Factories, the one door left open in the Qing. China\'s earliest mosque, its earliest foreign trading houses and most of its earliest emigrants started here.'],
'泉州': ['宋元时叫刺桐,是当时世界上最大的港口之一,马可·波罗与伊本·白图泰都写过它——伊斯兰教、印度教、摩尼教、基督教的遗迹至今叠在同一座城里。明代海禁之后港淤了,它才安静下来。',
 'Known as Zayton under the Song and Yuan, it was among the largest ports on earth, and both Marco Polo and Ibn Battuta wrote about it — remains of Islam, Hinduism, Manichaeism and Christianity still lie stacked in the one city. It fell quiet only after the Ming sea bans, when the harbour silted up.'],
'张掖': ['河西走廊最宽的一段绿洲,祁连山的雪水到这里摊开成一片好地,自古「金张掖」。汉朝设四郡时它叫张掖——取「张国臂掖,以通西域」,意思是伸出胳膊把西域揽过来:这个地名本身就是一句国策。','The widest stretch of oasis in the Hexi corridor, where meltwater off the Qilian mountains spreads into good farmland — "golden Zhangye" in the old phrase. The Han named it Zhangye, "to stretch out the arm and reach the Western Regions": the place name is itself a statement of policy.'],
'武威': ['河西走廊的东大门,进出中原的第一站,古称凉州。汉武帝取名「武威」,是要「彰显大汉的武功军威」;此后两千年里,谁想经营西域,都得先坐稳这里。','The eastern gate of the Hexi corridor and the first stop coming in from China proper, known of old as Liangzhou. Emperor Wu named it Wuwei, "martial might", and for two thousand years after, anyone who meant to hold the Western Regions had first to hold this place.'],
'敦煌': ['南边祁连山,北边戈壁沙漠,雪水从山上下来在中间浇出一串绿洲,连成一条一千多公里长、最窄处只有几十公里的通道——这就是河西走廊——中原西去,几乎只有这一条路好走。敦煌是这条路上的最后一个绿洲,出了这里就是沙漠:向西去的人在这儿补给,向东来的东西在这儿落脚。莫高窟一千年凿了七百多个洞,把这条路上往来过的所有信仰都画在了墙上。',
 'The Qilian mountains to the south, gravel desert to the north, and meltwater coming off the peaks to water a chain of oases between them: that chain, more than a thousand kilometres long and at its narrowest a few dozen wide, is the Hexi corridor: going west out of China proper, there is hardly another road worth taking. Dunhuang is its last oasis, with desert beyond: those heading west stocked up here, and what came east put down here first. Over a thousand years more than seven hundred caves were cut at Mogao, and every faith that ever passed along this road was painted on their walls.'],
'喀什': ['塔克拉玛干沙漠西缘的路口,南北两条丝路在这里合成一条,翻过帕米尔往西——所以它同时属于东亚、中亚和南亚,谁强盛就归谁。老城的土坯房与巴扎的样子,一千年没怎么变。',
 'The junction at the western edge of the Taklamakan, where the northern and southern Silk Roads join into one before crossing the Pamirs — which is why it belongs at once to East, Central and South Asia, and to whoever is strongest. The mud-brick lanes and the bazaar have changed little in a thousand years.'],
'拉萨': ['海拔三千六百米的河谷,是青藏高原上少数能种青稞、养得起一座城的地方——松赞干布把都城迁来,布达拉宫从此立在红山上。它是政教合一制度存续最久的一个中心。',
 'A valley at 3,600 metres, one of the few places on the Tibetan plateau where barley grows and a city can be fed — Songtsen Gampo moved his capital here and the Potala has stood on the red hill ever since. It is the longest-lasting centre of a state where religion and government were one.'],
'苏州': ['太湖东岸的水网,舟比车方便——春秋时是吴国都城,明清时是天下最富的地方之一。它把钱花在园林、丝绸、评弹和吃上,「苏式」两个字至今是精致的代名词。',
 'A web of water east of Lake Tai where boats beat carts — capital of the state of Wu in the Spring and Autumn period, and among the richest places in the empire under the Ming and Qing. It spent its money on gardens, silk, storytelling and food, and Suzhou-style still means refinement.'],
'大同': ['长城脚下,农耕与草原的接缝——北魏在这里建都近百年,把云冈石窟凿在城西的崖壁上。此后一千年它一直是九边重镇:守住大同,才守得住北京的西北门。',
 'At the foot of the Great Wall, on the seam between farmland and steppe — the Northern Wei ruled from here for nearly a century and cut the Yungang grottoes into the cliffs west of town. For the thousand years after, it was a frontier stronghold: hold Datong and you hold the northwest gate to Beijing.'],
'太原': ['汾河谷地的中心,进可下中原、退可守山西——李渊父子从这里起兵夺天下,唐朝把它称作「北都」。晋祠里的宋代彩塑和那几株周柏,是这座城最老的东西。',
 'The centre of the Fen river valley, from which one can strike into the central plain or fall back into the mountains of Shanxi — Li Yuan and his sons raised their army here and the Tang called it the northern capital. The Song painted figures and the ancient cypresses at the Jinci temple are the oldest things it keeps.'],
'长沙': ['湘江边上,楚文化的南方大本营——马王堆汉墓在这里出土了两千年不腐的女尸,以及世界上最早的帛书地图之一。近代它又送出了一批改变中国的人。',
 'On the Xiang river, the southern heartland of Chu culture — the Mawangdui tombs here yielded a woman\'s body uncorrupted after two thousand years, and among the earliest maps ever drawn on silk. In modern times it sent out a generation of people who changed China.'],
'香港': ['珠江口外的一个深水良港。它不是一夜之间冒出来的:唐代屯门已是广州的外港,宋代设官富盐场,明代属新安县。1841 年英国人来了之后的一百五十年,它成了中国与世界之间的那道闸门——资本、货物、消息和人,都从这条缝里进出;1997 年回归后,它仍是内地连着世界的一扇门。',
 'A deep-water harbour outside the Pearl River mouth. It did not appear overnight: Tuen Mun was already Guangzhou\'s outer port under the Tang, the Song ran a salt works here, and under the Ming it belonged to Xin\'an county. For the century and a half after the British came in 1841 it became the sluice gate between China and the world — capital, goods, news and people all passed through that gap — and since it returned to China in 1997 it remains a door between the mainland and the world.'],
'台北': ['淡水河与基隆河冲出的盆地,清末才正式建城——却在二十世纪成了中华文化保存与转化的一个特别现场:故宫南迁的一批文物、闽南与日式混生的街屋,以及一种影响整个华语世界的流行文化,都在这里。',
 'A basin scoured out by the Tamsui and Keelung rivers, only formally walled as a city in the late Qing — yet in the twentieth century it became a singular site where Chinese culture was both preserved and transformed: part of the imperial collection moved south, streets where Minnan and Japanese building styles grew together, and a popular culture that reached the whole Chinese-speaking world.'],
/* 东亚其余 · 东南亚 */
'乌兰巴托': ['色楞格河支流边的一座喇嘛寺,原本跟着活佛走、搬过二十多次家——1778 年才定下来。它是世界上最冷的首都,也是唯一一座由游牧传统直接长成的现代都会:一半人住楼房,一半人住蒙古包。',
 'It began as a monastery that moved with its living Buddha and shifted site more than twenty times before settling in 1778. The coldest capital on earth, and the only modern metropolis grown directly out of a nomadic tradition: half its people live in flats and half in gers.'],
'哈拉和林': ['窝阔台在鄂尔浑河谷建的都城,蒙古帝国从这里发号施令三十余年——教皇的使节、法国的银匠、波斯的工匠都在这里出现过。帝国重心南移之后它很快荒废,今天地面上主要是后来的额尔德尼召寺。',
 'Ögedei\'s capital in the Orkhon valley, from which the Mongol empire gave its orders for some thirty years — a papal envoy, a French silversmith and Persian craftsmen all turned up here. When the empire\'s centre moved south it was quickly abandoned; what stands today is mostly the later Erdene Zuu monastery.'],
'首尔': ['汉江边、北有北汉山,风水与防务都说得通——1394 年朝鲜王朝定都于此,此后六百年没换过。它是「小中华」到现代化的整条路径最完整的样本:景福宫、殖民时期的街区与今天的江南,叠在同一座城里。',
 'On the Han river with Bukhansan to the north, the site satisfied both geomancy and defence — the Joseon dynasty made it their capital in 1394 and never moved again. It is the fullest single sample of a route from Confucian kingdom to modern state: Gyeongbok palace, the colonial-era blocks and today\'s Gangnam all stacked in one city.'],
'平壤': ['大同江畔,朝鲜半岛有文字记载最早的城之一,乐浪郡与高句丽都以此为中心——它在半岛北部的地位,相当于汉江之于南部。1950 年代几乎被夷平,今天的城是按一张规划图重建出来的。',
 'On the Taedong river, among the earliest recorded cities on the peninsula and the centre of both the Lelang commandery and Goguryeo — it is to the north what the Han river is to the south. Levelled almost completely in the early 1950s, the city standing today was rebuilt to a single plan.'],
'东京': ['原名江户,不过是关东平原上的一个渔村与城下町——德川家康 1603 年在这里开幕府,把政治中心从京都搬了过来。它两次被彻底摧毁(1923 地震、1945 空袭),两次原地重建,是「毁了再来」这件事做得最彻底的城市。',
 'Once Edo, no more than a fishing village and castle town on the Kanto plain — Tokugawa Ieyasu set up his shogunate here in 1603 and moved the political centre away from Kyoto. Destroyed twice over, by the 1923 earthquake and the 1945 firebombing, and rebuilt in place both times: no city has done starting over more thoroughly.'],
'京都': ['794 年迁都至此,此后一千年是日本的都城——街道是照着唐长安的棋盘格画的,至今还能看出来。它没有被战争彻底毁掉,所以是日本保存最完整的一座古城:寺院、庭园、町屋与茶道的规矩,都在这里定型。',
 'The capital was moved here in 794 and stayed for a thousand years — the streets were laid out on the grid of Tang Chang\'an, and it still shows. It escaped total destruction in war, so it is Japan\'s most intact old city: temples, gardens, townhouses and the etiquette of tea all took their final form here.'],
'河内': ['红河三角洲的顶点,越南从这里向南展开——1010 年李朝迁都称升龙。它是东亚汉字文化圈最西南的一角:科举、律令与儒学在此扎根一千年,而法国人又在同一座城里留下了林荫大道与歌剧院。',
 'At the apex of the Red River delta, the point from which Vietnam unfolded southward — the Ly dynasty moved its capital here in 1010 and called it Thang Long. It is the southwestern corner of the East Asian world of Chinese characters, where examinations, law codes and Confucian learning took root for a thousand years, and where the French then left boulevards and an opera house.'],
'吴哥': ['洞里萨湖北岸的平原,靠一套巨大的水库与水渠储住季风雨——高棉人用这套水利养出百万人口的都城,再把国力浇进石头里。吴哥窟是世界上最大的宗教建筑;15 世纪都城南迁后,森林把它盖了四百年。',
 'On the plain north of the Tonle Sap, a vast system of reservoirs and canals held the monsoon rains — the Khmer used that water to feed a capital of perhaps a million people, then poured the surplus into stone. Angkor Wat is the largest religious structure on earth; after the capital moved south in the fifteenth century the forest covered it for four hundred years.'],
'曼谷': ['湄南河下游的沼泽地,1782 年才建都——却是东南亚唯一没有被殖民过的国家的首都。暹罗一面派人去欧洲学,一面把领土割给英法换来独立,这种「自己改」的路径,城市里看得见:王宫与摩天楼隔一条河。',
 'Swampland on the lower Chao Phraya, made a capital only in 1782 — yet the capital of the one Southeast Asian country never colonised. Siam sent people to study in Europe while ceding territory to Britain and France to buy its independence, and that path of reforming itself is visible in the city: palace and skyscrapers across one river from each other.'],
'蒲甘': ['伊洛瓦底江中游的干旱平原,11—13 世纪缅族在这里建国——两百年里造了一万多座佛塔,今天还剩三千多座立在平原上。蒙古人来过之后它衰落,但上座部佛教在缅甸的形态就是在这里定下的。',
 'On the dry plain of the middle Irrawaddy, where the Bamar founded their kingdom in the eleventh to thirteenth centuries — in two hundred years they built over ten thousand pagodas, and more than three thousand still stand. It declined after the Mongols came, but the shape Theravada Buddhism took in Burma was settled here.'],
'仰光': ['伊洛瓦底江三角洲的港口,英国人 1852 年之后把它建成殖民地首府——所以它有东南亚保存最完整的一片殖民时期建筑。而城中心的大金塔比这一切都早得多,是缅甸人自己的坐标。',
 'A port on the Irrawaddy delta which the British built into a colonial capital after 1852 — which is why it holds the most intact stretch of colonial-era architecture in Southeast Asia. The Shwedagon at its centre is far older than any of that, and is the Burmese people\'s own point of reference.'],
'马六甲': ['扼着马六甲海峡最窄处,从中国到印度的船必须经过——15 世纪的苏丹国靠收税与转口成为区域中心,伊斯兰教由此传遍群岛。此后葡、荷、英轮流占领它,街上至今是这几层叠着的。',
 'It commands the narrowest point of its strait, and ships between China and India had to pass — the fifteenth-century sultanate grew into a regional centre on tolls and transhipment, and Islam spread across the archipelago from here. The Portuguese, Dutch and British held it in turn, and the streets still show those layers stacked.'],
'雅加达': ['爪哇西北岸的港口,原名巽他格拉巴,1619 年荷兰人在此建巴达维亚,做了三百多年东印度公司的总部——今天它是东南亚最大的城市,也是世界上下沉最快的大城之一,印尼因此正在迁都。',
 'A port on Java\'s northwest coast, once Sunda Kelapa, where the Dutch founded Batavia in 1619 and ran the East India Company for three centuries — today it is Southeast Asia\'s largest city and one of the fastest-sinking on earth, which is why Indonesia is moving its capital.'],
'马尼拉': ['马尼拉湾的深水港,1571 年被西班牙人占领后成为大帆船贸易的东端——美洲的白银从这里进入中国,中国的丝绸瓷器从这里运往美洲,这条航线跑了二百五十年,是第一条真正的全球贸易线。',
 'A deep harbour on Manila Bay, taken by Spain in 1571 and made the eastern end of the galleon trade — American silver entered China here and Chinese silk and porcelain left for the Americas. That route ran for 250 years and was the first genuinely global trade line.'],
'巨港': ['穆西河边的内河港,离海足够近又足够安全——7 到 11 世纪三佛齐从这里控制马六甲海峡,靠收过路费而不是靠农业立国。义净在这里停留学梵文,说当时城中僧侣上千。',
 'A river port on the Musi, close enough to the sea and far enough to be safe — from the seventh to the eleventh century Srivijaya controlled the Straits of Malacca from here, living on tolls rather than farming. The pilgrim Yijing stopped to study Sanskrit and reported a thousand monks in the city.'],
'新加坡': ['马六甲海峡东端的一个岛,1819 年之前只是渔村与转口点——莱佛士把它设为自由港,此后两百年它一直靠同一件事活着:全世界的船在这里换货、加油、办手续。没有资源,只有位置。',
 'An island at the eastern end of the Straits, no more than fishing villages and a transhipment point before 1819 — Raffles declared it a free port and for two centuries it has lived on the same thing: the world\'s ships changing cargo, taking fuel and doing paperwork here. No resources, only position.'],
'吉隆坡': ['两条河交汇处的一个采锡矿点,1857 年才有人定居——华人矿工与英国殖民官把它从泥泞的矿区变成首府。它是少数由「挖矿」而不是由王朝或港口长出来的东南亚大城。',
 'A tin-mining spot where two rivers meet, first settled in 1857 — Chinese miners and British officials turned a muddy diggings into a capital. It is one of the few large Southeast Asian cities grown out of mining rather than out of a dynasty or a harbour.'],
'胡志明市': ['湄公河三角洲的门户,原属高棉、17 世纪起归越南——法国人把它建成「东方巴黎」,后来它做过南越首都。今天它是越南的经济中心,城里的天主教堂、骑楼与摩托车流,是这几段历史的叠加。',
 'The gateway to the Mekong delta, Khmer land until Vietnam took it from the seventeenth century — the French built it into the Paris of the East and it later served as the capital of South Vietnam. Now Vietnam\'s economic centre, where cathedral, shophouse arcades and rivers of motorbikes are those histories laid one on another.'],
/* 南亚 · 中亚 */
'德里': ['亚穆纳河边、恒河平原的西北门户,从开伯尔山口下来的军队都要在这里决胜负——所以同一片地上前后叠了七座「德里」。德里苏丹国与莫卧儿都定都于此,今天的印度政府也在这里。',
 'On the Yamuna at the northwest gate of the Ganges plain, where armies coming down from the Khyber had to settle matters — which is why seven successive Delhis lie stacked on the one site. The Delhi Sultanate and the Mughals both ruled from here, and so does India today.'],
'孟买': ['七个小岛被填成一片,英国人从葡萄牙人手里当嫁妆拿到——深水港加上打通内陆的铁路,让它取代了所有旧港。棉花、电影与金融三样东西在这里叠出印度最有钱也最拥挤的城。',
 'Seven islets filled in to make one land, handed to Britain by Portugal as part of a dowry — a deep harbour plus railways into the interior let it displace every older port. Cotton, cinema and finance stacked here into India\'s richest and most crowded city.'],
'摩亨佐达罗': ['印度河边的一座四千五百年前的城,有笔直的街道、砖砌下水道与统一规格的砖——这套规划水平在当时是世界级的。它没有王宫也没有神庙,统治方式至今没人说得清;文字也还没被释读。',
 'A city on the Indus of four and a half thousand years ago, with straight streets, brick drains and bricks of standard size — planning of a level unmatched anywhere then. It has no palace and no temple, and nobody can yet say how it was governed; its script remains unread.'],
'加尔各答': ['胡格利河边的三个村子,东印度公司 1690 年在此设商馆——后来做了英属印度的首都一百四十年。孟加拉文艺复兴、印度最早的大学与报纸都在这里发生,1786 年琼斯宣布梵语与欧洲语言同源,讲的也是这里。',
 'Three villages on the Hooghly where the East India Company opened a factory in 1690 — and which then served as the capital of British India for 140 years. The Bengal Renaissance, India\'s first universities and first newspapers all happened here, and it was here in 1786 that Jones announced Sanskrit\'s kinship with the languages of Europe.'],
'瓦拉纳西': ['恒河在这里向北拐一个弯,朝向太阳升起的方向——印度教徒认为在此地死去可以解脱轮回,所以河边的火葬台千年不熄。它是世界上持续有人居住的最古老城市之一,佛陀第一次说法的鹿野苑就在城外。',
 'The Ganges turns north here, toward the sunrise — Hindus hold that to die in this place breaks the cycle of rebirth, so the cremation ghats have not gone out in a thousand years. Among the oldest continuously inhabited cities on earth, with Sarnath, where the Buddha first taught, just outside it.'],
'拉合尔': ['旁遮普平原的中心,从中亚进入印度的必经之地——莫卧儿把它当作陪都,城堡与沙利马尔花园都在这里。1947 年分治,它一夜之间从印度的城变成巴基斯坦的城。',
 'The centre of the Punjab plain and the way into India from Central Asia — the Mughals treated it as a second capital and left the fort and the Shalimar gardens. In the 1947 partition it turned overnight from an Indian city into a Pakistani one.'],
'科伦坡': ['锡兰西南岸的天然良港,葡、荷、英轮流占领——但它真正的分量来自岛的位置:印度洋航线的中途站,阿拉伯、中国、欧洲的船都在这里停。锡兰的肉桂曾是欧洲最贵的香料之一。',
 'A natural harbour on Ceylon\'s southwest coast held in turn by the Portuguese, Dutch and British — but its weight comes from where the island sits: a way station on the Indian Ocean routes where Arab, Chinese and European ships all stopped. Ceylon cinnamon was once among the costliest spices in Europe.'],
'巴特那': ['恒河与三条支流的交汇处,古名华氏城——孔雀王朝与笈多王朝的都城,阿育王从这里发出向四方传法的使团。麦加斯梯尼说它当时是世界上最大的城,城墙有六百多座塔楼。',
 'Where the Ganges meets three tributaries; anciently Pataliputra — capital of the Maurya and the Gupta, and the place from which Ashoka sent his missions out in every direction. Megasthenes reported it the largest city in the world, its wall carrying more than six hundred towers.'],
'汉皮': ['图恩加巴德拉河边一片巨石荒原,毗奢耶那伽罗王朝在这里建都——15 世纪时人口可能仅次于北京,葡萄牙人说它「大得像罗马」。1565 年一场战败后被彻底洗劫,此后再无人重建,废墟就那样留在石头之间。',
 'A boulder-strewn waste by the Tungabhadra where Vijayanagara built its capital — in the fifteenth century perhaps second in population only to Beijing, and the Portuguese said it was as big as Rome. After a defeat in 1565 it was sacked completely and never rebuilt; the ruins simply stayed among the rocks.'],
'撒马尔罕': ['泽拉夫尚河的绿洲,丝路上南北东西四条路在这里交叉——粟特商人以此为家,把中国的丝与波斯的银运来运去。帖木儿把它建成帝国的橱窗,雷吉斯坦广场三面的经学院至今是中亚最漂亮的建筑。',
 'An oasis on the Zeravshan where four Silk Road branches crossed — the Sogdian merchants made it home and moved Chinese silk and Persian silver both ways. Timur built it into the shop window of his empire, and the three madrasas around the Registan are still the finest buildings in Central Asia.'],
'布哈拉': ['同一条河下游的另一座绿洲城,以学问著称——伊本·西那在这里进过王室藏书楼,《布哈里圣训实录》的编者也出自这里。萨曼王朝在此定都,波斯语文学在这一代重新站起来。',
 'Another oasis city downstream on the same river, known for learning — Ibn Sina got into the royal library here, and the compiler of the most authoritative hadith collection came from here. The Samanids made it their capital, and Persian literature stood up again in that generation.'],
'塔什干': ['天山西麓的绿洲,自古是草原与绿洲两个世界的集市——俄国 1865 年占领后把它建成中亚的行政中心,1966 年大地震后又整片重建。今天它是中亚人口最多的城市。',
 'An oasis on the western flank of the Tianshan, since ancient times the marketplace between the steppe world and the oasis world — Russia took it in 1865 and made it Central Asia\'s administrative centre, and after the 1966 earthquake it was rebuilt wholesale. It is now the most populous city in Central Asia.'],
'阿拉木图': ['天山北麓的果园地带,苹果的野生祖先就长在这一带的山里,城名意思正是「苹果之父」——19 世纪俄国设的哨所长成城市,苏联时代做过哈萨克首都,1997 年首都北迁后它仍是最大的城。',
 'Orchard country on the northern slope of the Tianshan, where the wild ancestor of the apple grows in the hills — the name means father of apples. A Russian fort of the nineteenth century grew into a city, served as the Kazakh capital in Soviet times, and remained the largest city after the capital moved north in 1997.'],
/* 中东 · 北非 */
'巴格达': ['底格里斯河边一块什么都不是的地方,曼苏尔 762 年在这里画了一座正圆的城——它随即成为世界最大的城市与阿拉伯科学的中心,智慧宫把希腊、波斯、印度的书全译成阿拉伯语。1258 年蒙古人破城,那批书大半没了。',
 'A spot on the Tigris that was nothing until al-Mansur drew a perfect circle there in 762 — it promptly became the largest city on earth and the centre of Arabic science, with the House of Wisdom translating Greek, Persian and Indian books into Arabic. The Mongols took it in 1258 and most of those books went with it.'],
'大马士革': ['东古塔绿洲靠一条河从沙漠里抠出来的城,自称世界上有人连续居住最久的城之一——它是倭马亚王朝的首都,清真寺是在一座教堂、更早是一座罗马神庙的地基上盖起来的,三层叠着,一目了然。',
 'A city scratched out of the desert by one river feeding the Ghouta oasis, and among the claimants to longest continuously inhabited on earth — capital of the Umayyads, its great mosque raised on the footings of a church and, below that, a Roman temple: three layers, plain to see.'],
'耶路撒冷': ['一座没有港口、没有大河、也不在商路上的山城——它的全部分量来自三个宗教都把最要紧的事安放在这几百米之内。正因为如此,它是世界上被围攻、被摧毁、被重建次数最多的城市之一。',
 'A hill town with no harbour, no great river and no place on a trade route — all its weight comes from three religions having put their most important things inside a few hundred metres. For exactly that reason it is among the most besieged, destroyed and rebuilt cities on earth.'],
'麦加': ['汉志山谷里一处有泉水的商站,古来就是阿拉伯部落的朝圣与休战之地——先知在此出生,天房成为全球穆斯林礼拜的方向。今天每年数百万人来朝觐,是世界上规模最大的定期人类集会。',
 'A caravan halt with a spring in a Hijaz valley, a place of pilgrimage and truce among Arab tribes long before Islam — the Prophet was born here and the Kaaba became the direction of prayer for Muslims everywhere. The hajj now draws millions a year, the largest regular gathering of people in the world.'],
'麦地那': ['绿洲农业养得起的一座城,先知 622 年迁来这里,伊斯兰历从那一年起算——第一个穆斯林共同体在此成形,政教合一的国家形态也是在这里第一次搭起来的。先知墓就在城中的清真寺里。',
 'An oasis city that farming could feed, to which the Prophet moved in 622 — the year from which the Islamic calendar counts. The first Muslim community took shape here, and here for the first time a state was built in which faith and government were one. The Prophet\'s tomb lies inside the mosque at its centre.'],
'伊斯坦布尔': ['金角湾与博斯普鲁斯之间的一个半岛,同时卡着欧亚陆桥和黑海航道——世界上唯一横跨两洲的大城。它做过罗马、拜占庭与奥斯曼三个帝国的首都,圣索菲亚从教堂改清真寺再改博物馆,把这段历史压成了一栋建筑。',
 'A peninsula between the Golden Horn and the Bosphorus, holding both the land bridge between continents and the sea road to the Black Sea — the only great city on two continents. Capital of the Roman, Byzantine and Ottoman empires in turn, and Hagia Sophia, church then mosque then museum, compresses that history into one building.'],
'特拉布宗': ['黑海南岸少数有良港又有山路通往内陆的地方——丝路最西的一段海路在这里上岸,转陆路去波斯。拜占庭覆灭后,一个特拉比松帝国在这里又撑了八年才被奥斯曼收走。',
 'One of the few places on the Black Sea\'s southern shore with both a harbour and a mountain road inland — the westernmost sea leg of the Silk Road came ashore here to go on to Persia overland. After Byzantium fell, an empire of Trebizond held out here eight years longer before the Ottomans took it.'],
'开罗': ['尼罗河从这里开始分叉成三角洲,上下埃及的接点——四千年里这一带换过好几个都城名字,法蒂玛王朝 969 年建的开罗是最后一个。爱资哈尔清真寺办的学校,是世界上仍在运作的最古老大学之一。',
 'Where the Nile begins to split into its delta, the joint between Upper and Lower Egypt — over four thousand years several capitals stood in this stretch, and the Cairo founded by the Fatimids in 969 was the last of them. The school at the al-Azhar mosque is among the oldest universities still working anywhere.'],
'亚历山大': ['亚历山大在尼罗河口西侧亲自选的城址,背海面湖、避开淤积——它成了地中海世界最大的港与最大的图书馆所在地。欧几里得在这里教书,埃拉托色尼在这里量出了地球的周长。',
 'Alexander chose the site himself west of the Nile mouth, sea before it and lake behind, clear of the silt — it became the Mediterranean\'s greatest port and the home of its greatest library. Euclid taught here, and here Eratosthenes measured the circumference of the earth.'],
'德黑兰': ['厄尔布尔士山南麓的一个小镇,1786 年才被恺加王朝选作首都——选它是因为离部族根据地近、又居中。二十世纪石油让它急速膨胀,今天是西亚人口最多的城市。',
 'A small town on the southern flank of the Alborz, chosen as capital by the Qajars only in 1786 — chosen because it was close to their tribal base and centrally placed. Oil swelled it fast in the twentieth century, and it is now the most populous city in western Asia.'],
'伊斯法罕': ['扎因代河边的绿洲,阿拔斯一世 1598 年迁都至此并按图纸重建——广场、清真寺、桥与花园一起规划,当时人说「伊斯法罕半天下」。它是伊斯兰世界少数由一次完整城市设计造出来的都城。',
 'An oasis on the Zayandeh river which Abbas I made his capital in 1598 and rebuilt to a drawing — square, mosques, bridges and gardens planned together, so that people said Isfahan is half the world. It is one of the few Islamic capitals produced by a single complete act of city design.'],
'巴比伦': ['幼发拉底河边的城,汉谟拉比在这里刻下法典,尼布甲尼撒在这里造起伊什塔尔门——「巴比伦」这个名字后来在西方成了一个象征,象征财富、混乱与骄傲。城早已成土丘,象征却一直在用。',
 'A city on the Euphrates where Hammurabi had his laws carved and Nebuchadnezzar raised the Ishtar Gate — the name later became a symbol in the West for wealth, confusion and pride. The city is long since a mound; the symbol is still in service.'],
'安卡拉': ['安纳托利亚高原中央的一个小城,以安哥拉羊毛出名——1923 年凯末尔把首都从伊斯坦布尔迁来这里,理由正是它平庸:不带帝国记忆,离海远、好防守,象征一个新国家从头开始。',
 'A small town in the middle of the Anatolian plateau, known for Angora wool — Atatürk moved the capital here from Istanbul in 1923 precisely because it was unremarkable: no imperial memory, far from the sea and defensible, a new country starting fresh.'],
'突尼斯': ['迦太基的近旁,湖与海之间的一道地峡——古城被罗马夷平之后,阿拉伯人在几公里外重建了突尼斯。麦地那老城是保存最好的伊斯兰城区之一,而二十世纪它成了整个北非现代化最早的样本之一。',
 'Next to Carthage, on an isthmus between lake and sea — after Rome razed the old city the Arabs rebuilt a few kilometres away as Tunis. Its medina is among the best preserved Islamic quarters anywhere, and in the twentieth century it became one of North Africa\'s earliest samples of modernisation.'],
'非斯': ['阿特拉斯山与里夫山之间的通道口,808 年建城——卡鲁因大学建于 859 年,是世界上持续办学最久的高等学府之一。老城两万条巷子不通车,至今按中世纪的样子运转。',
 'At the pass between the Atlas and the Rif, founded in 808 — the Qarawiyyin, established in 859, is among the longest continuously operating institutions of higher learning in the world. Cars cannot enter the old city\'s thousands of lanes, which still work as they did in the Middle Ages.'],
'喀布尔': ['兴都库什山南麓的谷地,从中亚进印度的必经隘口就在旁边——所以亚历山大、贵霜、莫卧儿、英国人、苏联人、美国人都来过。它的位置决定了它的命运:永远是别人路上的一站。',
 'A valley on the southern side of the Hindu Kush, beside the pass that anyone going from Central Asia into India must use — so Alexander, the Kushans, the Mughals, the British, the Soviets and the Americans all came. Its position has decided its fate: forever a stage on somebody else\'s road.'],
'迪拜': ['波斯湾边一个靠采珍珠和转口过活的小港,1960 年代人口还不到十万——石油钱不多,所以它把钱押在港口、机场与免税区上。今天全球最长的航线在这里换乘,这是一座靠「中转」重新发明自己的城。',
 'A small Gulf port living on pearling and transhipment, with under a hundred thousand people in the 1960s — it had little oil money, so it staked what it had on a port, an airport and free zones. The world\'s longest flights now connect here: a city that reinvented itself out of being a place to change planes.'],
/* 欧洲 */
'雅典': ['阿提卡半岛贫瘠多山,种不出足够的粮,却有银矿与好港——所以雅典人只能出海:换粮、殖民、造舰队。公民大会、悲剧、哲学与陪审团制度,都在这块养不活自己的地方长出来。',
 'Attica is stony and hilly and cannot grow enough grain, but it had silver and a good harbour — so Athenians had to go to sea to trade for food, to plant colonies and to build a fleet. The assembly, tragedy, philosophy and the jury court all grew on land that could not feed itself.'],
'罗马': ['台伯河上第一个能徒步涉过的地方,又在七座山丘上易守——一个渡口小镇由此长成横跨三洲的帝国中心。它把「城市」这个词的含义定了下来:道路、引水渠、法律与公民身份,都从这里往外发。',
 'The first place the Tiber could be forded, and seven hills to hold — a river-crossing town grew from that into the centre of an empire across three continents. It fixed what the word city means: roads, aqueducts, law and citizenship all went out from here.'],
'巴黎': ['塞纳河中的一个小岛,四面是水的天然堡垒,又卡在南北陆路与东西水路的交叉点——罗马人叫它卢泰西亚。它把「首都」做到极致:法国的行政、语言、学术与时尚标准,一千年来都由这一座城定。',
 'An islet in the Seine, a natural fortress with water on every side, sitting where the north-south road crosses the east-west river — the Romans called it Lutetia. It took the idea of a capital to its limit: for a thousand years France\'s administration, language, learning and taste have all been set in this one city.'],
'伦敦': ['泰晤士河感潮段的上限——海船能上来、桥又架得起来,罗马人因此在这里设城。后来它靠同一个优势成了世界最大的港与金融中心:格林尼治的那条本初子午线,就是这个位置带来的话语权。',
 'The head of the Thames tideway — seagoing ships could come up and a bridge could still be thrown across, which is why the Romans put a city here. The same advantage later made it the world\'s largest port and financial centre, and the prime meridian at Greenwich is what that position bought.'],
'马德里': ['伊比利亚半岛正中央的高原,没有大河也没有港——1561 年被选作首都,理由恰恰是「谁也不偏」。它是欧洲海拔最高的首都之一,也是少数纯粹因为行政居中而被造出来的大城。',
 'A plateau in the exact middle of Iberia, with no great river and no port — chosen as capital in 1561 precisely because it favoured nobody. One of Europe\'s highest capitals, and one of the few large cities made purely because it was administratively central.'],
'科尔多瓦': ['瓜达尔基维尔河边,10 世纪时是西欧最大的城市——后倭马亚王朝在这里建起大清真寺与几十座图书馆,阿拉伯语、希伯来语与拉丁语的学者同城工作。欧洲后来读到的亚里士多德,不少是经由这里译回去的。',
 'On the Guadalquivir, and in the tenth century the largest city in western Europe — the later Umayyads raised the great mosque and dozens of libraries here, and scholars working in Arabic, Hebrew and Latin shared the town. A good deal of the Aristotle Europe later read came back through this place.'],
'里斯本': ['特茹河口的深水港,面朝大西洋而不是地中海——这个朝向在 15 世纪突然变成优势:向南沿非洲海岸摸索的航线从这里出发,达伽马也从这里去印度。欧洲的海洋时代是从这个河口开始的。',
 'A deep harbour at the mouth of the Tagus facing the Atlantic rather than the Mediterranean — an orientation that turned into an advantage in the fifteenth century: the voyages feeling their way south along Africa set out from here, and so did da Gama for India. Europe\'s ocean age began at this river mouth.'],
'柏林': ['施普雷河边的沼泽沙地,本来毫无优势——普鲁士把它一步步造成首都,再由它统一德国。二十世纪它两次成为世界的裂缝:第三帝国的中心,以及被一道墙劈成两半的城。',
 'Marsh and sand by the Spree, with no natural advantage at all — Prussia built it into a capital step by step, and from it unified Germany. Twice in the twentieth century it became the world\'s fault line: the centre of the Third Reich, and a city split in two by a wall.'],
'维也纳': ['多瑙河从这里冲出阿尔卑斯与喀尔巴阡之间的缺口,进入匈牙利平原——罗马人在此设营,哈布斯堡把它做成中欧的中心。1529 与 1683 两次奥斯曼围城都在这里被挡住,这条线因此成了欧洲的一道边界。',
 'The Danube breaks through the gap between the Alps and the Carpathians here and enters the Hungarian plain — the Romans camped here and the Habsburgs made it the centre of central Europe. Two Ottoman sieges, in 1529 and 1683, were stopped at this spot, and the line became one of Europe\'s borders.'],
'布拉格': ['伏尔塔瓦河的一个河湾,四面丘陵环抱——查理四世 14 世纪把它建成神圣罗马帝国的首都,中欧第一所大学也在这里。它几乎没被战争摧毁过,所以整座老城是欧洲少见的完整中世纪样本。',
 'A bend of the Vltava ringed by hills — Charles IV made it the capital of the Holy Roman Empire in the fourteenth century and founded central Europe\'s first university here. It was almost never destroyed in war, so the old town is a rare complete medieval sample.'],
'华沙': ['维斯瓦河边平原上的一座城,处在东西两大势力之间,无险可守——1944 年被系统性地夷平了八成以上。战后波兰人照着战前的画与照片把老城一砖一瓦重建,这件事本身成了它的身份。',
 'A city on the plain by the Vistula, caught between two great powers with nothing to defend it — in 1944 more than eighty per cent of it was systematically levelled. After the war Poles rebuilt the old town brick by brick from prewar paintings and photographs, and that act became its identity.'],
'斯德哥尔摩': ['梅拉伦湖流入波罗的海的那道水口,十四个岛上的城——控制这里就控制了瑞典内陆与海洋之间的门。铁与铜从内陆运出,城市因此起家;今天它是北欧最大的都会。',
 'At the outlet where Lake Mälaren runs into the Baltic, a city on fourteen islands — hold this and you hold the door between Sweden\'s interior and the sea. Iron and copper went out from the interior and made the city; today it is the largest metropolis in the Nordic countries.'],
'莫斯科': ['莫斯科河边的一座小公国,四周是森林,没有山也没有海——它的崛起靠的是替蒙古人收税、然后一点点吞并邻居。「第三罗马」的说法从这里出来,俄罗斯的中心此后一直没离开过这里太久。',
 'A small principality on the Moskva, surrounded by forest, with neither mountains nor sea — it rose by collecting taxes for the Mongols and then swallowing its neighbours one at a time. The claim to be the third Rome came from here, and the centre of Russia has never stayed away from it for long.'],
'基辅': ['第聂伯河边的高岸,「从瓦良格到希腊」的水路在此设关——罗斯诸公国的第一个中心,988 年在这里受洗,东斯拉夫世界的东正教信仰由此开始。这座城的历史归属,至今仍是争论的核心。',
 'High banks on the Dnieper where the route from the Varangians to the Greeks was controlled — the first centre of the Rus principalities, baptised in 988, and the beginning of Orthodox Christianity in the East Slavic world. Whose history this city belongs to is still argued about.'],
'阿姆斯特丹': ['阿姆斯特尔河上的一道水坝,城名就是这个意思——全城建在木桩上,靠运河排水。17 世纪它是世界金融的中心:第一家把股票公开卖给公众的公司、第一个证券交易所、第一次金融泡沫,都发生在这里。',
 'A dam on the Amstel, which is exactly what the name says — the whole city stands on wooden piles and drains through canals. In the seventeenth century it was the centre of world finance: the first company to sell its shares to the public, the first stock exchange and the first financial bubble all happened here.'],
'威尼斯': ['潟湖里的一片泥滩,躲避蛮族的人跑到这里定居——没有农田,只能靠海。它把「做中间人」做成了国家:垄断东西方贸易六百年,复式记账、海上保险与国债都在这里成形。',
 'Mudflats in a lagoon where people fleeing invaders settled — no farmland, so the sea was the only living. It turned being the middleman into a state: six centuries monopolising trade between East and West, and double-entry bookkeeping, marine insurance and government bonds all took shape here.'],
'佛罗伦萨': ['阿尔诺河谷里一座靠羊毛与银行起家的城——美第奇家族把赚来的钱花在艺术上,文艺复兴因此有了资金。城不大,但但丁、乔托、布鲁内莱斯基、达芬奇、米开朗基罗都在这条河边工作过。',
 'A city in the Arno valley that made its money in wool and banking — the Medici spent it on art, and that is what funded the Renaissance. It is not large, yet Dante, Giotto, Brunelleschi, Leonardo and Michelangelo all worked by this river.'],
'米兰': ['波河平原的中心,阿尔卑斯山几条隘口的南端出口——罗马时代就是西帝国的都城之一,米兰敕令在这里颁布。它此后一直是意大利的工业与商业首都,而不是政治首都。',
 'The centre of the Po plain at the southern end of several Alpine passes — a capital of the Western Roman Empire, and the place from which the Edict of Milan was issued. Ever since it has been Italy\'s industrial and commercial capital rather than its political one.'],
'巴塞罗那': ['地中海西岸的港口,背后是山、面前是海,与马德里隔着整个半岛——加泰罗尼亚的语言、工业与自治传统都以此为中心。高迪把这座城变成了一个建筑实验场。',
 'A Mediterranean port with mountains behind and sea in front, the whole peninsula away from Madrid — the centre of Catalonia\'s language, industry and tradition of self-rule. Gaudí turned the city into a laboratory of building.'],
/* 撒南非洲 */
'廷巴克图': ['尼日尔河大弯的北岸,骆驼商队与河船在这里换手——南边的黄金换北边的盐,这个交换点养出了一座学问之城。桑科雷的经学院与私人藏书在 16 世纪已有数万册手稿,至今仍在抢救。',
 'On the north bank of the Niger bend, where camel caravans and river boats changed hands — gold from the south for salt from the north, and that exchange grew a city of learning. The Sankore madrasa and private libraries held tens of thousands of manuscripts by the sixteenth century, and the rescue of them is still going on.'],
'加奥': ['尼日尔河边的另一个渡口,桑海帝国的都城——阿斯基亚·穆罕默德从这里统治西非最大的一个国家,直到 1591 年摩洛哥人带着火枪穿过撒哈拉把它打垮。',
 'Another crossing on the Niger and the capital of the Songhai empire — Askia Muhammad ruled West Africa\'s largest state from here until 1591, when a Moroccan force with firearms came across the Sahara and broke it.'],
'卡诺': ['萨赫勒地带的商站,豪萨诸城邦里最大的一个——跨撒哈拉商路的南端终点,以染布和皮革出名,城墙圈起的面积在 15 世纪已很可观。它是西非伊斯兰学问的一个中心。',
 'A trading town in the Sahel and the largest of the Hausa city-states — the southern terminus of the trans-Saharan routes, known for its dye pits and leather, and already walled around a considerable area by the fifteenth century. It is one of the centres of Islamic learning in West Africa.'],
'金沙萨': ['刚果河下游最后一段可通航水域的尽头,再往下就是瀑布——所以货物必须在这里上岸转陆路。这个断点造出了一座城,今天它是世界上最大的法语城市之一。',
 'At the end of the last navigable stretch of the lower Congo, with rapids below — so cargo had to come ashore here and go on by land. That break in the river made a city, and it is now among the largest French-speaking cities in the world.'],
'阿克苏姆': ['埃塞俄比亚高原北部,控制着红海到内陆的商路——阿克苏姆王国 4 世纪就皈依基督教,是世界上最早的基督教国家之一,还自己铸币。那些整块花岗岩凿成的方尖碑至今立在原地。',
 'On the northern Ethiopian highlands, controlling the road from the Red Sea inland — the kingdom of Aksum adopted Christianity in the fourth century, among the earliest states anywhere to do so, and minted its own coins. Its obelisks, each cut from a single block of granite, still stand where they were raised.'],
'亚的斯亚贝巴': ['海拔两千四百米的高原新城,1886 年才建——却成了非洲统一组织与非盟的总部所在地。埃塞俄比亚是非洲唯一没有被长期殖民的国家,这个身份让这座年轻的城成了整个大陆的政治客厅。',
 'A new city on a plateau at 2,400 metres, founded only in 1886 — yet it became the seat of the Organisation of African Unity and then the African Union. Ethiopia is the one African country never subjected to lasting colonial rule, and that standing turned this young city into the continent\'s political drawing room.'],
'大津巴布韦': ['赞比西河与林波波河之间的高原,金矿与牧场都在附近——11 到 15 世纪这里用不加灰浆的干砌石墙建起大围场,墙高十一米、周长两百多米。它证明撒南非洲有过自己的石构城市文明。',
 'On the plateau between the Zambezi and the Limpopo, with gold and grazing both nearby — between the eleventh and fifteenth centuries a great enclosure was raised here in mortarless dry stone, walls eleven metres high and over two hundred metres around. It is the proof that sub-Saharan Africa had a stone-built urban civilisation of its own.'],
'蒙巴萨': ['东非海岸的深水港,靠季风来去——阿拉伯、波斯、印度与中国的船在这里停,斯瓦希里语就是这样一种混出来的语言。郑和的船队到过这一带,葡萄牙人后来在这里建了耶稣堡。',
 'A deep harbour on the East African coast worked by the monsoon — Arab, Persian, Indian and Chinese ships put in here, and Swahili is the language that mixture produced. Zheng He\'s fleets reached this coast, and the Portuguese later built Fort Jesus here.'],
'基尔瓦': ['坦桑尼亚外海的一座小岛,13—15 世纪是斯瓦希里海岸最富的城邦——它控制着南边索法拉的黄金出口。伊本·白图泰称它是他见过最美的城之一;大清真寺的珊瑚石穹顶至今还在。',
 'A small island off Tanzania and the richest of the Swahili city-states in the thirteenth to fifteenth centuries — it controlled the gold coming out of Sofala to the south. Ibn Battuta called it one of the finest cities he had seen, and the coral-stone domes of its great mosque still stand.'],
'拉各斯': ['潟湖与海之间的沙洲,原是约鲁巴人的渔村与后来的奴隶贸易港——独立后成为尼日利亚的首都与经济中心。今天它是非洲人口最多的城市,也是非洲流行文化输出最猛的地方。',
 'Sandbars between lagoon and sea, once Yoruba fishing settlements and later a slaving port — after independence it became Nigeria\'s capital and economic centre. It is now the most populous city in Africa and the hardest-hitting exporter of African popular culture.'],
'开普敦': ['好望角内侧的桌湾,荷兰东印度公司 1652 年在这里设补给站——绕过非洲去亚洲的船必须在此加水加菜。这个「中途站」的性质定了它此后的一切:多族群、多语言,以及漫长的种族隔离。',
 'Table Bay inside the Cape of Good Hope, where the Dutch East India Company set up a resupply station in 1652 — ships rounding Africa for Asia had to take on water and greens here. Being a way station decided everything after: many peoples, many languages, and a long apartheid.'],
'麦罗埃': ['尼罗河第五与第六瀑布之间,库施王国的都城——这一带有铁矿也有燃料,冶铁规模在非洲罕见。麦罗埃人自己的文字至今没有被完全释读,城外那片小而陡的金字塔比埃及的更多。',
 'Between the fifth and sixth cataracts of the Nile, capital of the kingdom of Kush — with both iron ore and fuel at hand, its ironworking was on a scale rare in Africa. The Meroitic script has still not been fully read, and the small steep pyramids outside the city outnumber those of Egypt.'],
'内罗毕': ['东非大裂谷东侧的高地,1899 年因为铁路才有这个点——英国人要一个凉爽、无疟疾的中转站。它由此长成东非最大的城,联合国在发展中国家设的两个总部之一就在这里。',
 'Highland on the eastern side of the Rift Valley, existing as a point on the map only because of the railway in 1899 — the British wanted a cool, malaria-free staging post. It grew from that into East Africa\'s largest city, and holds one of only two UN headquarters in the developing world.'],
'约翰内斯堡': ['1886 年在这片高原上发现了世界上最大的金矿脉,几年内荒野变成城——它是非洲少数几座完全由采矿造出来的大城,种族隔离时期的城市规划至今还刻在它的地图上。',
 'In 1886 the world\'s largest gold reef was found on this plateau and within a few years veld had become a city — one of the few great African cities made entirely by mining, and the planning of the apartheid years is still written into its map.'],
/* 美洲 */
'墨西哥城': ['原本是特斯科科湖中的一座岛城特诺奇蒂特兰,阿兹特克人用浮田在湖上种地——西班牙人把湖填了,在废墟上照原位盖起主教座堂与总督府。今天全城因为抽干的湖床而年年下沉。',
 'It began as Tenochtitlan, an island city in Lake Texcoco where the Mexica farmed on floating plots — the Spanish drained the lake and raised cathedral and palace on the ruins, in the same spot. The whole city now sinks a little every year into that emptied lakebed.'],
'特奥蒂瓦坎': ['墨西哥谷地北端,公元 1 至 6 世纪美洲最大的城市,人口十万以上——街道按一条「亡者大道」严格对齐,太阳金字塔与月亮金字塔立在两端。谁建的、说什么语言,至今没有定论;阿兹特克人来时它已废弃八百年,是他们给了这个名字。',
 'At the north end of the valley of Mexico, the largest city in the Americas from the first to the sixth century, with over a hundred thousand people — its streets align strictly on an avenue the Aztecs later called the road of the dead, with the pyramids of the Sun and Moon at either end. Who built it and what they spoke is still unsettled; it had been abandoned eight hundred years when the Aztecs arrived and named it.'],
'奇琴伊察': ['尤卡坦半岛没有地表河流,雨水直接渗进石灰岩——所以城建在天然井(cenote)旁边,那既是水源也是祭祀之地。库库尔坎金字塔的台阶总数正好是一年的天数,春分日影会在栏边爬出一条蛇。',
 'Yucatan has no surface rivers; rain sinks straight into the limestone — so the city was built beside natural wells, which were both its water and its place of sacrifice. The steps of the Kukulcan pyramid add up to the days of a year, and at the equinox the shadow crawls down the balustrade as a serpent.'],
'蒂卡尔': ['佩滕雨林深处的玛雅大城,靠人工蓄水池撑过每年的旱季——神庙尖顶高过树冠,是这片森林里唯一的地标。9 世纪玛雅低地诸城相继被弃,原因至今在争,长期干旱是主要嫌疑之一。',
 'A great Maya city deep in the Peten forest, carried through each dry season by man-made reservoirs — its temple combs rise above the canopy, the only landmarks in that forest. In the ninth century the lowland Maya cities were abandoned one after another; the cause is still argued, with prolonged drought the leading suspect.'],
'库斯科': ['安第斯山中三千四百米的谷地,印加人称之为「世界的肚脐」——四条大道从这里通向帝国四方,整座城据说是按美洲豹的形状规划的。西班牙人拆了神庙,却拆不动那些不用灰浆、严丝合缝的巨石墙基。',
 'A valley at 3,400 metres in the Andes which the Inca called the navel of the world — four highways ran from here to the empire\'s four quarters, and the city is said to have been laid out in the shape of a puma. The Spanish pulled down the temples but could not shift the mortarless megalithic footings, still fitted so tightly that a blade will not enter.'],
'利马': ['秘鲁沿海的沙漠上,一条河流出安第斯山的地方——皮萨罗 1535 年选在这里建城,因为靠海便于与西班牙联系。此后两百多年,南美洲的白银都从这里的港口运走。',
 'On the coastal desert of Peru where a river comes out of the Andes — Pizarro founded the city here in 1535 because the sea kept him in touch with Spain. For more than two centuries afterwards, South America\'s silver left through its port.'],
'波哥大': ['安第斯山东支上一片两千六百米高的平原,原是穆伊斯卡人的中心——「黄金国」的传说就出自他们在附近湖中投金的仪式。西班牙人在此建城,今天它是南美海拔最高的大都会之一。',
 'A plain at 2,600 metres on the eastern range of the Andes, once the heartland of the Muisca — the legend of El Dorado came from their ritual of casting gold into a nearby lake. The Spanish founded a city here, and it is now among the highest large metropolises in South America.'],
'布宜诺斯艾利斯': ['拉普拉塔河口的平原,背后是潘帕斯草原——牛肉与小麦从这里装船运往欧洲,十九世纪末的移民潮又把整船整船的意大利人和西班牙人卸在这里。探戈就是在这个码头区混出来的。',
 'A plain at the mouth of the Rio de la Plata with the pampas behind — beef and wheat were loaded here for Europe, and the immigration of the late nineteenth century unloaded shiploads of Italians and Spaniards. The tango was mixed together in these dock districts.'],
'里约热内卢': ['瓜纳巴拉湾,群山直插进海——葡萄牙王室 1808 年为躲拿破仑整个搬到这里,使它一度成为唯一一座欧洲帝国设在美洲的首都。这段经历让巴西的独立走了一条与西属美洲完全不同的路。',
 'Guanabara Bay, where the mountains come straight down into the sea — the Portuguese royal family moved here bodily in 1808 to escape Napoleon, briefly making it the only European imperial capital in the Americas. That episode sent Brazil to independence by a wholly different road from Spanish America.'],
'圣地亚哥': ['安第斯山与海岸山脉之间的一条中央谷地,气候像地中海——西班牙人 1541 年建城于此。狭长的智利就是沿着这条谷地展开的,全国一半人口住在这座城的周围。',
 'A central valley between the Andes and the coastal range, with a Mediterranean climate — the Spanish founded the city here in 1541. Long thin Chile unfolds along that valley, and half the country lives around this one city.'],
'哈瓦那': ['加勒比海最好的一个瓶颈形港湾,进出口都窄、里面宽——西班牙的运银船队每年在此集结再一同横渡大西洋。这个「集合点」的角色让它有了整个美洲最坚固的一批要塞。',
 'The finest bottleneck harbour in the Caribbean, narrow at the mouth and wide within — Spain\'s treasure fleets gathered here each year before crossing the Atlantic together. Being the assembly point gave it some of the strongest fortifications in the Americas.'],
'卡霍基亚': ['密西西比河与密苏里河交汇附近的肥沃泛滥平原,玉米北传之后长出北美最大的聚落——僧侣丘是墨西哥以北最大的史前土方工程,用篮子一筐一筐堆起来。1350 年前后被弃,原因至今没有定论。',
 'Fertile floodplain near where the Mississippi meets the Missouri, where the northward spread of maize grew the largest settlement in North America — Monks Mound is the biggest earthwork north of Mexico, raised basketload by basketload. It was abandoned around 1350 and why is still unsettled.'],
'纽约': ['哈得孙河口的一个深水良港,不冻、又能一直通到内陆——1825 年伊利运河修通后,中西部的货物全从这里出海,它由此甩开所有对手。自由女神像立在港口入口,一亿人的祖先从这里上岸。',
 'A deep, ice-free harbour at the mouth of the Hudson with a way inland — after the Erie Canal opened in 1825 the produce of the Midwest went to sea through it and it left every rival behind. The Statue of Liberty stands at the harbour mouth, where the ancestors of a hundred million people came ashore.'],
'洛杉矶': ['南加州的一片半干旱盆地,本地水根本不够——它是靠一条二百多公里的引水渠从东边山谷抢来的水才长起来的。电影业选择这里是因为阳光和地形多样,一个盆地里能拍出全世界。',
 'A semi-arid basin in southern California with nowhere near enough local water — it grew only by taking water through an aqueduct more than two hundred kilometres from a valley to the east. The film industry chose it for the sunlight and the variety of terrain: one basin that could stand in for the whole world.'],
'旧金山': ['金门海峡内侧的大海湾,1848 年发现黄金之后一年之内人口涨了二十倍——淘金、铁路与后来的硅谷,三次都是同一件事:全世界想碰运气的人往这里跑。',
 'The great bay inside the Golden Gate, where the population rose twentyfold in the year after gold was found in 1848 — the gold rush, the railroad and later Silicon Valley were three versions of one thing: people from everywhere coming to try their luck.'],
'芝加哥': ['密歇根湖南端,五大湖水系与密西西比水系在这里几乎相接——一条运河把两大水系接通,美国的粮食与牲畜由此集散。1871 年大火烧光全城,重建时催生了世界上第一批钢框架高层建筑。',
 'At the southern end of Lake Michigan, where the Great Lakes and Mississippi watersheds nearly touch — a canal joined them, and America\'s grain and livestock moved through as a result. The fire of 1871 burned the city down, and the rebuilding produced the world\'s first steel-framed towers.'],
'西雅图': ['普吉特湾的深水港,背靠雪山面朝太平洋——木材与渔业起家,阿拉斯加淘金时做补给港,二战后靠飞机制造,再后来是软件与网络零售。同一个港口,四轮不同的行业。',
 'A deep harbour on Puget Sound with snow peaks behind and the Pacific in front — it began on timber and fishing, outfitted the Klondike gold rush, built aircraft after the war, and then made software and online retail. One harbour, four different industries in turn.'],
'华盛顿': ['波托马克河边一片沼泽地,1790 年由南北双方妥协选定——刻意不放在任何一个州里,也刻意不做商业中心。它是少数为了「当首都」而从零规划出来的城市,街道按朗方的图纸放射排列。',
 'Marshland on the Potomac, chosen in 1790 as a compromise between north and south — deliberately inside no state, and deliberately not a commercial centre. It is one of the few cities planned from nothing solely to be a capital, its avenues radiating along L\'Enfant\'s drawing.'],
'波士顿': ['一个被半岛护住的深港,清教徒 1630 年在此登陆——北美第一所大学、第一份报纸、第一个公立学校都在这里。美国独立的头几件事也都发生在这几条街上。',
 'A deep harbour sheltered by a peninsula where the Puritans landed in 1630 — North America\'s first college, first newspaper and first public school were all here. So were the first acts of American independence, on these same few streets.'],
'迈阿密': ['佛罗里达半岛南端的沙洲与湿地,1896 年铁路修到才建市——它是美国离拉丁美洲最近的大城,古巴革命之后的移民潮把它变成了一座西班牙语和英语并行的城。',
 'Sandbars and wetland at the tip of Florida, incorporated only when the railway arrived in 1896 — the American city closest to Latin America, and the exodus after the Cuban revolution turned it into a place where Spanish and English run side by side.'],
'多伦多': ['安大略湖北岸的一处天然良港,又是通往内陆的旧皮毛商路口——二十世纪后半叶它取代蒙特利尔成为加拿大的经济中心。今天全城约一半居民出生在国外,是世界上最多元的大城之一。',
 'A natural harbour on the north shore of Lake Ontario at the old fur-trade portage inland — in the second half of the twentieth century it displaced Montreal as Canada\'s economic centre. About half its residents were born abroad, making it one of the most diverse large cities anywhere.'],
'蒙特利尔': ['圣劳伦斯河上航行的终点,再往上就是激流——所以货物必须在这里换船,皮毛贸易的整个北美内陆网络由此展开。它是北美最大的法语城市,两种语言的张力塑造了加拿大的政治。',
 'The head of navigation on the St Lawrence, with rapids above — cargo had to change boats here, and the whole North American fur-trade network unfolded from that. It is the largest French-speaking city in North America, and the tension between its two languages has shaped Canadian politics.'],
'温哥华': ['落基山与太平洋之间的一条窄地,横贯大陆的铁路 1887 年通到这里——它是加拿大面向亚洲的门。北美西岸少数不冻的深水港之一,今天亚洲移民占人口的很大一部分。',
 'A narrow strip between the Rockies and the Pacific where the transcontinental railway arrived in 1887 — Canada\'s door to Asia. One of the few ice-free deep-water ports on the North American west coast, with Asian immigrants now a large share of its people.'],
/* 大洋洲 */
'悉尼': ['杰克逊港是世界上最大的天然良港之一,1788 年第一舰队就是在这里靠岸的——澳大利亚的欧洲史从这个海湾开始,而这块地上原本住着伊欧拉人。今天它是南半球最大的城市之一。',
 'Port Jackson is among the largest natural harbours on earth, and it was here that the First Fleet came ashore in 1788 — European Australia begins at this inlet, on land that belonged to the Eora. It is now one of the largest cities in the southern hemisphere.'],
'墨尔本': ['亚拉河口的平地,1835 年才有第一批定居者——1851 年维多利亚发现黄金,十年内人口涨了七倍,一度是世界上最富的城市之一。那批金子盖起来的宽街与排屋,至今是这座城的骨架。',
 'Flat land at the mouth of the Yarra with its first settlers only in 1835 — gold was found in Victoria in 1851, the population rose sevenfold in a decade and for a time it was among the richest cities in the world. The wide streets and terraces that gold paid for are still the city\'s skeleton.'],
'奥克兰': ['两个海湾之间一条狭窄的地峡,两边都能出海——毛利人早就看中这里,称之为「百情人之地」,因为值得为它争夺。全城建在约五十座火山锥上,是世界上人口最多的波利尼西亚人城市。',
 'A narrow isthmus between two harbours, with the sea reachable on both sides — Maori saw its worth long ago and called it the place desired by many, because it was worth fighting for. The city sits on some fifty volcanic cones and holds more Polynesian people than any other on earth.'],
'奥斯陆': ['挪威的首都,藏在一条一百公里长的峡湾尽头:维京人的船从这片水域出发,1049 年国王在这里建镇,后来在丹麦治下沉寂了几百年,1814 年重新做挪威的首都,1905 年成为独立王国的首都。三条维京长船原物就收藏在这里,它也是每年颁诺贝尔和平奖的城市。',
 'The capital of Norway sits at the head of a fjord a hundred kilometres long: Viking ships set out from these waters, a king founded the town in 1049, and after centuries in the shadow of Danish rule it became Norway\'s capital again in 1814 and the capital of an independent kingdom in 1905. Three real Viking longships are kept here, and it is the city where the Nobel Peace Prize is handed out each year.'],
'哥本哈根': ['丹麦的首都,守着波罗的海的出口厄勒海峡——名字的意思就是「商人港」。维京时代它周围是丹麦王国的核心,1167 年筑堡建城,15 世纪起做首都;17 世纪的克里斯蒂安四世给它盖了一堆塔楼与宫殿。今天它以自行车、运河边的彩色房子和小美人鱼像出名,2000 年一座跨海大桥把它和瑞典连在了一起。',
 'The capital of Denmark guards the Øresund, the gateway to the Baltic — the name means merchants\' harbour. In the Viking Age the heart of the Danish kingdom lay around it; a fort was built in 1167, and it became the capital in the fifteenth century, with Christian IV adding towers and palaces in the seventeenth. Today it is known for bicycles, coloured houses along the canals and the Little Mermaid, and since 2000 a bridge across the sound has tied it to Sweden.'],
};
